WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:04.870
Speaker 1: There is a very interesting new
poll out, a 2024 poll in which Joe Biden is

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.700
leading Donald Trump by six.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:08.720
Now, why do we care about that?

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:10.330
It's September of 2022.

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:12.130
Well, there are a number of different reasons.

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:18.849
One is that like no election, I can remember,
we are already sort of in the 2024 election.

00:00:18.849 --> 00:00:24.210
And usually each election is a very kind of
compartmentalized with very clear boundaries

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:25.210
election.

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:28.839
And in this case, it is very different as
much of what is already happening now bears

00:00:28.839 --> 00:00:30.529
directly on 2024.

00:00:30.529 --> 00:00:34.180
It's also something we care about because
Donald Trump's refrain has been, I'm winning

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:35.370
every poll.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:37.850
Now, we don't know if Trump is running.

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:39.399
We don't know if Joe Biden is running.

00:00:39.399 --> 00:00:44.140
So what it would even mean to lead a poll
is a question, but it is not true that Donald

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:45.929
Trump is leading every poll.

00:00:45.929 --> 00:00:46.989
Let's take a look.

00:00:46.989 --> 00:00:52.859
The Hill reporting new poll shows Biden with
six point lead on Trump.

00:00:52.859 --> 00:00:59.120
Biden is leading Trump by six in a hypothetical
2024 presidential matchup, new polling shows

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:06.240
in a Yahoo News YouGov poll released yesterday,
Wednesday, 48% of registered voters said they'd

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:11.080
vote Biden if the election were today, and
42% say they'd vote Trump.

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:16.470
Now, that's only 90% of the electorate, meaning
there's still another 10% in flux.

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:19.170
That is often the case in these polls.

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:26.600
Biden held a three point lead in the hypothetical
2020 rematch in August from August to September.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:29.399
Biden's lead has gone from 3 to 6.

00:01:29.399 --> 00:01:33.590
